doc:sec-11-2-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "11(3) Entity definitions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Each of the following is an excluded entity: (aa) the National Data Commissioner and any APS employee made available to the National Data Commissioner under section 47; (a) the National Anti-Corruption Commission; (ab) the Inspector of the National Anti-Corruption Commission; (b) the agency known as the Australian Criminal Intelligence Commission established by the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002; (ba) the Australian Federal Police; (c) that part of the Defence Department known as the Australian Geospatial-Intelligence Organisation; (d) the Australian National Audit Office; (e) the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; (f) the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation; (g) the Australian Signals Directorate; (h) that part of the Defence Department known as the Defence Intelligence Organisation;  Chapter 1  Preliminary" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-11a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "11A The data sharing project"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-11a ;
    values:originalText "Project, and output and ADSP-enhanced data of project (1) A project involves at least both of the following elements: (a) an entity (the sharer) shares data with another entity (the user), either directly or through another entity (the intermediary); (b) the user collects the data and uses the output of the project, which is: (i) the copy of the data collected by the user; and (ii) any data that is the result or product of the user’s use of the shared data.  Preliminary  Chapter 1 Definitions  Part 1.2  Section 11A Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 Note 1: The sharer’s authorisation to share data is in section 13. The user’s authorisation to collect and use data is in section 13A. Note 2: A project may involve sharing of data by multiple sharers, if multiple entities are data custodians of the data. (2) If, for the purposes of sharing data under section 13, data services are performed in relation to data, or data is created, by or on behalf of the sharer, the project also involves performing the services or creating the data. (3) If the sharer shares data with the user through an intermediary, the project also involves both of the following elements: (a) the sharer shares the data with the intermediary; (b) the intermediary collects the data and uses the ADSP-enhanced data of the project, which is: (i) the copy of the data collected by the intermediary; and (ii) any data that is the result or product of the intermediary’s use of the shared data. Note: The sharer’s authorisation to share data with the intermediary, and the intermediary’s authorisation to share data with the user on behalf of the sharer, are in section 13. The intermediary’s authorisation to collect data from the sharer and use it is in section 13B. (4) If the sharer is provided with access to output or ADSP-enhanced data of the project, the project also involves the sharer’s collection and use of the output or ADSP-enhanced data. Note: The sharer’s authorisation to collect and use the output or ADSP-enhanced data of the project is in section 13C. Combining projects (5) A data sharing agreement may treat multiple projects as a single project, as long as they all have the same data sharing purpose or purposes and the same sharer and user and (if applicable) intermediary.  Chapter 1  Preliminary" ;
    skos:definition "Project, and output and ADSP-enhanced data of project (1) A project involves at least both of the following elements: (a) an entity (the sharer) shares data with another entity (the user), either directly or through another entity (the intermediary); (b) the user collects the data and uses the output of the project, which is: (i) the copy of the data collected by the user; and (ii) any data that is the result or product of the user’s use of the shared data.  Preliminary  Chapter 1 Definitions  Part 1.2  Section 11A Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 Note 1: The sharer’s authorisation to share data is in section 13. The user’s authorisation to collect and use data is in section 13A. Note 2: A project may involve sharing of data by multiple sharers, if multiple entities are data custodians of the data. (2) If, for the purposes of sharing data under section 13, data services are performed in relation to data, or data is created, by or on behalf of the sharer, the project also involves performing the services or creating the data. (3) If the sharer shares data with the user through an intermediary, the project also involves both of the following elements: (a) the sharer shares the data with the intermediary; (b) the intermediary collects the data and uses the ADSP-enhanced data of the project, which is: (i) the copy of the data collected by the intermediary; and (ii) any data that is the result or product of the intermediary’s use of the shared data. Note: The sharer’s authorisation to share data with the intermediary, and the intermediary’s authorisation to share data with the user on behalf of the sharer, are in section 13. The intermediary’s authorisation to collect data from the sharer and use it is in section 13B. (4) If the sharer is provided with access to output or ADSP-enhanced data of the project, the project also involves the sharer’s collection and use of the output or ADSP-enhanced data. Note: The sharer’s authorisation"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "45986c8621efd5756cc54105b00517ae9f7b85d0c16c7fc51eb132e79740dc0a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-11a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-11a-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-11a-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-11a-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-11a-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf> ;
    dc:source "data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf, p.24" .
doc:sec-11a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "11A The data sharing project" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Project, and output and ADSP-enhanced data of project (1) A project involves at least both of the following elements: (a) an entity (the sharer) shares data with another entity (the user), either directly or through another entity (the intermediary); (b) the user collects the data and uses the output of the project, which is: (i) the copy of the data collected by the user; and (ii) any data that is the result or product of the user’s use of the shared data.  Preliminary  Chapter 1 Definitions  Part 1.2  Section 11A Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 Note 1: The sharer’s authorisation to share data is in section 13. The user’s authorisation to collect and use data is in section 13A. Note 2: A project may involve sharing of data by multiple sharers, if multiple entities are data custodians of the data. (2) If, for the purposes of sharing data under section 13, data services are performed in relation to data, or data is created, by or on behalf of the sharer, the project also involves performing the services or creating the data. (3) If the sharer shares data with the user through an intermediary, the project also involves both of the following elements: (a) the sharer shares the data with the intermediary; (b) the intermediary collects the data and uses the ADSP-enhanced data of the project, which is: (i) the copy of the data collected by the intermediary; and (ii) any data that is the result or product of the intermediary’s use of the shared data. Note: The sharer’s authorisation to share data with the intermediary, and the intermediary’s authorisation to share data with the user on behalf of the sharer, are in section 13. The intermediary’s authorisation to collect data from the sharer and use it is in section 13B. (4) If the sharer is provided with access to output or ADSP-enhanced data of the project, the project also involves the sharer’s collection and use of the output or ADSP-enhanced data. Note: The sharer’s authorisation to collect and use the output or ADSP-enhanced data of the project is in section 13C. Combining projects (5) A data sharing agreement may treat multiple projects as a single project, as long as they all have the same data sharing purpose or purposes and the same sharer and user and (if applicable) intermediary.  Chapter 1  Preliminary" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

