concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-16f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16F Compliance with APP-equivalence term"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-16f ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an entity is subject to an APP-equivalence term of a data sharing agreement, an act or practice of the entity that contravenes the term in relation to an individual is taken to be: (a) an interference with the privacy of the individual for the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988; and (b) covered by sections 13, 13G and 13H of that Act. Note: An act or practice that is an interference with privacy may be the subject of a complaint under section 36 of the Privacy Act 1988. (2) The entity is taken, for the purposes of Part V of the Privacy Act 1988 and any other provision of that Act that relates to that Part, to be an organisation (within the meaning of that Act) if: (a) an act or practice of the entity has contravened, or may have contravened, the APP-equivalence term in relation to an individual; and (b) the act or practice is the subject of a complaint to, or an investigation by, the Information Commissioner under Part V of the Privacy Act 1988.  Authorisations  Chapter 2 Privacy protections  Part 2.4  Section 16F Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), the reference in sections 13G and 13H of the Privacy Act 1988 to an entity includes a reference to any entity that is subject to an APP-equivalence term. (4) Paragraph 33C(1)(a) of the Privacy Act 1988 applies in relation to an entity that is subject to an APP-equivalence term of a data sharing agreement as if the entity were an APP entity. (5) Sections 80V and 80W of the Privacy Act 1988 apply in relation to an APP-equivalence term as if the term were a provision of that Act.  Chapter 2  Authorisations" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an entity is subject to an APP-equivalence term of a data sharing agreement, an act or practice of the entity that contravenes the term in relation to an individual is taken to be: (a) an interference with the privacy of the individual for the purposes of the Privacy Act 1988; and (b) covered by sections 13, 13G and 13H of that Act. Note: An act or practice that is an interference with privacy may be the subject of a complaint under section 36 of the Privacy Act 1988. (2) The entity is taken, for the purposes of Part V of the Privacy Act 1988 and any other provision of that Act that relates to that Part, to be an organisation (within the meaning of that Act) if: (a) an act or practice of the entity has contravened, or may have contravened, the APP-equivalence term in relation to an individual; and (b) the act or practice is the subject of a complaint to, or an investigation by, the Information Commissioner under Part V of the Privacy Act 1988.  Authorisations  Chapter 2 Privacy protections  Part 2.4  Section 16F Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), the reference in sections 13G and 13H of the Privacy Act 1988 to an entity includes a reference to any entity that is subject to an APP-equivalence term. (4) Paragraph 33C(1)(a) of the Privacy Act 1988 applies in relation to an entity that is subject to an APP-equivalence term of a data sharing agreement as if the entity were an APP entity. (5) Sections 80V and 80W of the Privacy Act 1988 apply in relation to an APP-equivalence term as if the term were a provision of that Act.  Chapter 2  Authorisations"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5aacab153ddbe735e42dc861dc251cfa91f12183635b19538a7ff2f85d42740a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-16f-ss-1 ;
