doc:sec-20b-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20B(1) Allowed access: providing access to output for validation or" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The data sharing agreement may allow the accredited user to provide another entity with access to specified output of the project, if the agreement: (a) allows the access to be provided to: (i) an entity that carries on a business, or is a not-for-profit entity, to which the output relates, for the purpose of validating or correcting the output; or (ii) an individual to whom the output relates, or a responsible person (within the meaning of the Privacy  Authorisations  Chapter 2 Allowed access to output of project  Part 2.7  Section 20C Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 Act 1988) for such an individual, for the purpose of validating or correcting the output; or (iii) another person in circumstances prescribed by the rules that relate to validating or correcting the output; and (b) requires the data custodian of the source data to be satisfied, before access is provided, that the access will be an authorised use of the output under section 13A." ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-20b-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20B(2) Allowed access: providing access to output for validation or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-20b-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If data exits the data sharing scheme under subsection 20E(2) as a result of the accredited user providing an entity, individual or other person with access to the data as allowed by subsection (1), the accredited user is taken to have collected a copy of the data from the entity, individual or person concerned, at the time the entity, individual or person validates or corrects the data." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If data exits the data sharing scheme under subsection 20E(2) as a result of the accredited user providing an entity, individual or other person with access to the data as allowed by subsection (1), the accredited user is taken to have collected a copy of the data from the entity, individual or person concerned, at the time the entity, individual or person validates or corrects the data."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b570f1a120bae896d2fbc7b6dd3cc4d29221b7676cb66a11580336146e0488e5" ;
    values:partOf concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-20b ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Collecting a copy of data from an entity upon validation or correction" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf> ;
    dc:source "data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf, p.60" ;
