concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-43 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "43 Advice related functions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-43 ;
    values:originalText "For the purposes of paragraph 42(1)(a), the Commissioner’s advice related functions are to do the following, on request by the Minister or on the Commissioner’s own initiative:  National Data Commissioner and National Data Advisory Council  Chapter 4 National Data Commissioner  Part 4.2 Establishment, functions and powers  Division 1 Section 44 Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (a) advise on matters relating to the operation of this Act, including Commonwealth laws and changes to Commonwealth laws relating to this Act; (aa) advise a data scheme entity about how, in the Commissioner’s opinion, the data sharing scheme applies, or would apply in particular circumstances, in relation to the entity; (ab) advise the Minister in relation to the exercise of the Minister’s powers under Part 5.2 (accreditation framework); (b) inform the Minister about actions to be taken by data scheme entities in order to comply with this Act; (c) report and make recommendations to the Minister in relation to this Act, or the need for or desirability of legislative or administrative action in relation to this Act." ;
    skos:definition "For the purposes of paragraph 42(1)(a), the Commissioner’s advice related functions are to do the following, on request by the Minister or on the Commissioner’s own initiative:  National Data Commissioner and National Data Advisory Council  Chapter 4 National Data Commissioner  Part 4.2 Establishment, functions and powers  Division 1 Section 44 Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (a) advise on matters relating to the operation of this Act, including Commonwealth laws and changes to Commonwealth laws relating to this Act; (aa) advise a data scheme entity about how, in the Commissioner’s opinion, the data sharing scheme applies, or would apply in particular circumstances, in relation to the entity; (ab) advise the Minister in relation to the exercise of the Minister’s powers under Part 5.2 (accreditation framework); (b) inform the Minister about actions to be taken by data scheme entities in order to comply with this Act; (c) report and make recommendations to the Minister in relation to this Act, or the need for or desirability of legislative or administrative action in relation to this Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "31bec9b4e92594ccfa3276a29c2fefa4569c2a63c863f1e11421986b3ef8bf6d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "78"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Commissioner must provide advice on matters related to the operation of the Act." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf> ;
    dc:source "data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf, p.78" ;
    cml:asserts concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-43-norm .
