doc:sec-74-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "74(1) Accreditation" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an entity applies for accreditation as an ADSP or an accredited user under section 76, the accreditation authority for the entity may grant the entity the accreditation applied for if: (a) the entity is an Australian entity and not an excluded entity; and (b) the authority is satisfied that the entity meets the criteria for accreditation under section 77, to a standard appropriate for the accreditation; and (c) the authority considers it appropriate, in all the circumstances, to grant the accreditation." ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer .

concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-74-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "74(2) Accreditation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-74-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the accreditation authority grants the entity the accreditation applied for, the authority may accredit the entity: (a) without imposing conditions of accreditation; or (b) with conditions of accreditation imposed by the authority, if the authority is satisfied that imposing the conditions is: (i) appropriate for reasons of security, including on the basis of an adverse or qualified security assessment in respect of a person; or (ii) otherwise reasonable and appropriate in the circumstances to ensure that scheme data is collected and used in accordance with this Act. Note 1: The accreditation authority must give the entity notice before making a decision to grant accreditation with conditions (see section 79). Note 2: Even if the accreditation authority does not impose conditions of accreditation, conditions of accreditation prescribed by the rules may still be applicable to the entity.  Regulation and enforcement  Chapter 5 Accreditation framework  Part 5.2 Accreditation  Division 1 Section 75 Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024" ;
    skos:definition "(2) If the accreditation authority grants the entity the accreditation applied for, the authority may accredit the entity: (a) without imposing conditions of accreditation; or (b) with conditions of accreditation imposed by the authority, if the authority is satisfied that imposing the conditions is: (i) appropriate for reasons of security, including on the basis of an adverse or qualified security assessment in respect of a person; or (ii) otherwise reasonable and appropriate in the circumstances to ensure that scheme data is collected and used in accordance with this Act. Note 1: The accreditation authority must give the entity notice before making a decision to grant accreditation with conditions (see section 79). Note 2: Even if the accreditation authority does not impose conditions of accreditation, conditions of accreditation prescribed by the rules may still be applicable to the entity.  Regulation and enforcement  Chapter 5 Accreditation framework  Part 5.2 Accreditation  Division 1 Section 75 Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "845bf6c548cbc5881ad769244067e3d8348f429d7751ee8eddf11e8e2d59f1f7" ;
    values:partOf concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-74 ;
    cof:pageNumber "94"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authority may accredit entity with or without conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
