concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-76 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "76 Application for accreditation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-76 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An entity may apply for accreditation, as an ADSP or an accredited user, to the accreditation authority for the entity. (2) The application must: (a) be made by an authorised officer on behalf of the entity; and (b) be in the form approved by the Commissioner (if any); and (c) include the evidence prescribed by the rules to support the criteria for accreditation and the entity’s ability to meet the criteria to the appropriate standard; and (d) include consent for the Commissioner to: (i) obtain information relevant to the entity’s application for accreditation from third parties; and (ii) verify information provided by the entity with third parties." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An entity may apply for accreditation, as an ADSP or an accredited user, to the accreditation authority for the entity. (2) The application must: (a) be made by an authorised officer on behalf of the entity; and (b) be in the form approved by the Commissioner (if any); and (c) include the evidence prescribed by the rules to support the criteria for accreditation and the entity’s ability to meet the criteria to the appropriate standard; and (d) include consent for the Commissioner to: (i) obtain information relevant to the entity’s application for accreditation from third parties; and (ii) verify information provided by the entity with third parties."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cc07e33bcc7fd8dcf2ab3e596583c69ce5b31bdecb8238f4d3cfef6e8b67b7b0" ;
    cof:pageNumber "96"^^xsd:integer ;
