doc:sec-77a-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "77A(3) General provisions relating to accreditation" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Accreditation is granted on the basis that: (a) under Part 5.2, the entity may be accredited with conditions of accreditation and conditions of accreditation may be imposed, varied or removed while the entity is accredited; and (b) the accreditation may be suspended or cancelled under section 81; and (c) the accreditation may be cancelled, revoked, terminated or varied, and conditions of accreditation may be imposed, varied or removed, by or under later legislation; and (d) no compensation is payable in any of those events.  Chapter 5  Regulation and enforcement" ;
    cof:pageNumber "97"^^xsd:integer .

concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-77b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "77B Conditions of accreditation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-77b ;
    values:originalText "(1) The rules may prescribe conditions of accreditation applicable to all entities, or to classes of entities, as prescribed. (2) Conditions of accreditation, whether prescribed by the rules or imposed by an accreditation authority under section 74, 78 or 84, may require or permit an entity to do something, or prevent it from doing something. (3) Examples of conditions that may be prescribed or imposed are conditions to do any of the following: (a) limit the individuals who may collect and use data; (b) require the entity to provide, at a specified time or specified intervals, evidence of specified matters, or specified information, relating to the entity’s accreditation; (c) prohibit collection or use of personal information; (d) prohibit collection and use of data other than by means of a secure access data service; (e) prohibit the entity from storing or accessing, or providing access to, scheme data outside Australia; (f) if the entity is, or is applying for accreditation as, an ADSP— limit the kinds of data services the entity may provide." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The rules may prescribe conditions of accreditation applicable to all entities, or to classes of entities, as prescribed. (2) Conditions of accreditation, whether prescribed by the rules or imposed by an accreditation authority under section 74, 78 or 84, may require or permit an entity to do something, or prevent it from doing something. (3) Examples of conditions that may be prescribed or imposed are conditions to do any of the following: (a) limit the individuals who may collect and use data; (b) require the entity to provide, at a specified time or specified intervals, evidence of specified matters, or specified information, relating to the entity’s accreditation; (c) prohibit collection or use of personal information; (d) prohibit collection and use of data other than by means of a secure access data service; (e) prohibit the entity from storing or accessing, or providing access to, scheme data outside Australia; (f) if the entity is, or is applying for accreditation as, an ADSP— limit the kinds of data services the entity may provide."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9e4f963330fc8b8c0ee53f76a3815961b61919f680f5c0cf8b64d52b7c1b6587" ;
    cof:pageNumber "98"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-77b-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-77b-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-77b-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf> ;
    dc:source "data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf, p.98" .
