doc:sec-83a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "83A Lifting of suspension" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If an entity’s accreditation is suspended under section 81, the accreditation authority for the entity may lift the suspension by written notice to the entity if satisfied that: (a) there are no longer any grounds for the suspension; or (b) it is otherwise no longer appropriate for the accreditation to be suspended.  Regulation and enforcement  Chapter 5 Accreditation framework  Part 5.2 Renewal of accreditation of ADSPs  Division 4 Section 84 Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024" ;
    cof:pageNumber "106"^^xsd:integer .

concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-84 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "84 Renewal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-84 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an entity applies for the renewal of the entity’s accreditation as an ADSP under section 85A, the Commissioner may grant the renewal if: (a) the entity is an Australian entity and not an excluded entity; and (b) the Commissioner is satisfied that the entity meets the criteria for accreditation under section 77, to a standard appropriate for accreditation as an ADSP; and (c) the Commissioner considers it appropriate, in all the circumstances, to grant the renewal. (2) If the Commissioner grants the renewal, the Commissioner may renew the accreditation: (a) without imposing conditions of accreditation on the entity; or (b) with conditions of accreditation imposed by the Commissioner (including conditions of accreditation imposed before the renewal that continue to be imposed on the entity), if the Commissioner is satisfied that imposing the conditions is: (i) appropriate for reasons of security, including on the basis of an adverse or qualified security assessment in respect of a person; or (ii) otherwise reasonable and appropriate in the circumstances to ensure that scheme data is collected and used in accordance with this Act. Note 1: The Commissioner must give the entity notice before making a decision to renew the entity’s accreditation with conditions (see section 79). Note 2: Even if the Commissioner does not impose conditions of accreditation, conditions of accreditation prescribed by the rules may still be applicable to the entity.  Chapter 5  Regulation and enforcement" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an entity applies for the renewal of the entity’s accreditation as an ADSP under section 85A, the Commissioner may grant the renewal if: (a) the entity is an Australian entity and not an excluded entity; and (b) the Commissioner is satisfied that the entity meets the criteria for accreditation under section 77, to a standard appropriate for accreditation as an ADSP; and (c) the Commissioner considers it appropriate, in all the circumstances, to grant the renewal. (2) If the Commissioner grants the renewal, the Commissioner may renew the accreditation: (a) without imposing conditions of accreditation on the entity; or (b) with conditions of accreditation imposed by the Commissioner (including conditions of accreditation imposed before the renewal that continue to be imposed on the entity), if the Commissioner is satisfied that imposing the conditions is: (i) appropriate for reasons of security, including on the basis of an adverse or qualified security assessment in respect of a person; or (ii) otherwise reasonable and appropriate in the circumstances to ensure that scheme data is collected and used in accordance with this Act. Note 1: The Commissioner must give the entity notice before making a decision to renew the entity’s accreditation with conditions (see section 79). Note 2: Even if the Commissioner does not impose conditions of accreditation, conditions of accreditation prescribed by the rules may still be applicable to the entity.  Chapter 5  Regulation and enforcement"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66ce93f5ddb4210a4fa4af5def3fb28b703d40dd8db54bda192736859d395bbc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "107"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-84-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-84-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
