    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the Commissioner grants the renewal, the Commissioner may renew the accreditation: (a) without imposing conditions of accreditation on the entity; or (b) with conditions of accreditation imposed by the Commissioner (including conditions of accreditation imposed before the renewal that continue to be imposed on the entity), if the Commissioner is satisfied that imposing the conditions is: (i) appropriate for reasons of security, including on the basis of an adverse or qualified security assessment in respect of a person; or (ii) otherwise reasonable and appropriate in the circumstances to ensure that scheme data is collected and used in accordance with this Act. Note 1: The Commissioner must give the entity notice before making a decision to renew the entity’s accreditation with conditions (see section 79). Note 2: Even if the Commissioner does not impose conditions of accreditation, conditions of accreditation prescribed by the rules may still be applicable to the entity.  Chapter 5  Regulation and enforcement" ;
