concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "85 Notice of renewal decision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-85 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner must give the entity written notice of the Commissioner’s decision under section 84, as soon as practicable after making the decision. (2) If the Commissioner grants the entity the renewal, the notice must set out the following: (a) the 5-year period for which the renewed accreditation is in effect (see paragraph 81(8)(a)); (b) if the Commissioner decides to grant the renewal with conditions of accreditation imposed by the Commissioner (including conditions of accreditation imposed before the renewal that continue to be imposed on the entity): (i) those conditions; and (ii) the reasons for the decision; and (iii) the entity’s review rights under Part 6.2. (3) If the Commissioner refuses to renew the entity’s accreditation, the notice must set out the following: (a) the reason for the refusal;  Regulation and enforcement  Chapter 5 Accreditation framework  Part 5.2 Renewal of accreditation of ADSPs  Division 4 Section 85A Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (b) that the entity’s accreditation will be suspended or cancelled under section 81; and (c) the entity’s review rights under Part 6.2." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner must give the entity written notice of the Commissioner’s decision under section 84, as soon as practicable after making the decision. (2) If the Commissioner grants the entity the renewal, the notice must set out the following: (a) the 5-year period for which the renewed accreditation is in effect (see paragraph 81(8)(a)); (b) if the Commissioner decides to grant the renewal with conditions of accreditation imposed by the Commissioner (including conditions of accreditation imposed before the renewal that continue to be imposed on the entity): (i) those conditions; and (ii) the reasons for the decision; and (iii) the entity’s review rights under Part 6.2. (3) If the Commissioner refuses to renew the entity’s accreditation, the notice must set out the following: (a) the reason for the refusal;  Regulation and enforcement  Chapter 5 Accreditation framework  Part 5.2 Renewal of accreditation of ADSPs  Division 4 Section 85A Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (b) that the entity’s accreditation will be suspended or cancelled under section 81; and (c) the entity’s review rights under Part 6.2."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fb20f1d4b76f8a567319d36bf4ff4af16a4cd093f81b05ec90c767c09dda855c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "108"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85-ss-3 ;
