doc:sec-85-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "85(1) Notice of renewal decision" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner must give the entity written notice of the Commissioner’s decision under section 84, as soon as practicable after making the decision." ;
    cof:pageNumber "108"^^xsd:integer .

concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "85(2) Notice of renewal decision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-85-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If the Commissioner grants the entity the renewal, the notice must set out the following: (a) the 5-year period for which the renewed accreditation is in effect (see paragraph 81(8)(a)); (b) if the Commissioner decides to grant the renewal with conditions of accreditation imposed by the Commissioner (including conditions of accreditation imposed before the renewal that continue to be imposed on the entity): (i) those conditions; and (ii) the reasons for the decision; and (iii) the entity’s review rights under Part 6.2." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If the Commissioner grants the entity the renewal, the notice must set out the following: (a) the 5-year period for which the renewed accreditation is in effect (see paragraph 81(8)(a)); (b) if the Commissioner decides to grant the renewal with conditions of accreditation imposed by the Commissioner (including conditions of accreditation imposed before the renewal that continue to be imposed on the entity): (i) those conditions; and (ii) the reasons for the decision; and (iii) the entity’s review rights under Part 6.2."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b796910f413213639e82d7d0c1bf0ac8df96e9ad4f99dd295ee741f3bfa32b02" ;
    values:partOf concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85 ;
    cof:pageNumber "108"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notice of renewal decision must provide specific information." ;
    dc:description "(a) the 5-year period for which the renewed accreditation is in effect; (b) if the Commissioner decides to grant the renewal with conditions of accreditation imposed by the Commissioner..." ;
