doc:sec-85-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "85(3) Notice of renewal decision" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the Commissioner refuses to renew the entity’s accreditation, the notice must set out the following: (a) the reason for the refusal;  Regulation and enforcement  Chapter 5 Accreditation framework  Part 5.2 Renewal of accreditation of ADSPs  Division 4 Section 85A Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (b) that the entity’s accreditation will be suspended or cancelled under section 81; and (c) the entity’s review rights under Part 6.2." ;
    cof:pageNumber "108"^^xsd:integer .

concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "85A Application for renewal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-85a ;
    values:originalText "(1) An entity that is accredited as an ADSP may apply to the Commissioner for renewal of its accreditation. Note: For the consequences of failure to apply for renewal, see subsection 81(8). An entity may apply for renewal under this section before or after its accreditation has been suspended under that subsection. (2) The application must: (a) be made by an authorised officer of the entity; and (b) be in the approved form (if any); and (c) include the evidence prescribed by the rules to support the criteria for accreditation and the entity’s ability to meet the criteria to the appropriate standard; and (d) include consent for the Commissioner to: (i) obtain information relevant to the entity’s application for renewal from third parties; and (ii) verify information provided by the entity with third parties.  Chapter 5  Regulation and enforcement" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An entity that is accredited as an ADSP may apply to the Commissioner for renewal of its accreditation. Note: For the consequences of failure to apply for renewal, see subsection 81(8). An entity may apply for renewal under this section before or after its accreditation has been suspended under that subsection. (2) The application must: (a) be made by an authorised officer of the entity; and (b) be in the approved form (if any); and (c) include the evidence prescribed by the rules to support the criteria for accreditation and the entity’s ability to meet the criteria to the appropriate standard; and (d) include consent for the Commissioner to: (i) obtain information relevant to the entity’s application for renewal from third parties; and (ii) verify information provided by the entity with third parties.  Chapter 5  Regulation and enforcement"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "accc600ec71e2b72382300518b0d163edb9df1f746cb790ddc6de727078dbb04" ;
    cof:pageNumber "109"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-85a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
