    cof:title "125A(1) Contraventions by entities of civil penalty provisions and other" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) In determining whether an entity has contravened a civil penalty provision of this Act, or otherwise breached this Act: (a) the entity is taken to have engaged in any conduct engaged in:  Other matters  Chapter 6 Extension of authorisations and attribution of conduct  Part 6.3  Section 125A Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 (i) by a designated individual for the entity, if the conduct is within the actual or apparent scope of the individual’s designation; or (ii) by a body corporate that is party to an approved contract with the entity, if the conduct is within the actual or apparent scope of the approved contract; and (b) if it is necessary to establish the entity’s state of mind, it is sufficient to establish the state of mind of an individual who has engaged in conduct as mentioned in subparagraph (a)(i)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer .

concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-125a-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "125A(2) Contraventions by entities of civil penalty provisions and other"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-125a-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Despite subsection (1), a government entity does not contravene a civil penalty provision of this Act because of conduct that is attributed to the entity under subsection (1), if the entity took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct. Note: The government entity bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (2) (see section 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Despite subsection (1), a government entity does not contravene a civil penalty provision of this Act because of conduct that is attributed to the entity under subsection (1), if the entity took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct. Note: The government entity bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (2) (see section 96 of the Regulatory Powers Act)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "51a2b3a363b80c0cb1dfd356499fb920cf4a1a2abbd857964f236e3d121cf2b5" ;
    values:partOf concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-125a ;
    cof:pageNumber "142"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Government entity bears evidential burden to prove reasonable precautions were taken." ;
    dc:description "Evidence of due diligence" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
