concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-141 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "141 Commonwealth not liable to pay a fee"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-141 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commonwealth is not liable to pay a fee that is payable under this Act. However, it is the Parliament’s intention that the Commonwealth should be notionally liable to pay such a fee. (2) The Finance Minister may give such written directions as are necessary or convenient for carrying out or giving effect to subsection (1) and, in particular, may give directions in relation to  Other matters  Chapter 6 Other matters  Part 6.5  Section 142 Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 the transfer of money within an account, or between accounts, operated by the Commonwealth. (3) Directions under subsection (2) have effect, and must be complied with, despite any other Commonwealth law. (4) In subsections (1) and (2), Commonwealth includes a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013) that cannot be made liable to taxation by a Commonwealth law." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commonwealth is not liable to pay a fee that is payable under this Act. However, it is the Parliament’s intention that the Commonwealth should be notionally liable to pay such a fee. (2) The Finance Minister may give such written directions as are necessary or convenient for carrying out or giving effect to subsection (1) and, in particular, may give directions in relation to  Other matters  Chapter 6 Other matters  Part 6.5  Section 142 Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022 Compilation date: 11/12/2024 the transfer of money within an account, or between accounts, operated by the Commonwealth. (3) Directions under subsection (2) have effect, and must be complied with, despite any other Commonwealth law. (4) In subsections (1) and (2), Commonwealth includes a Commonwealth entity (within the meaning of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013) that cannot be made liable to taxation by a Commonwealth law."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "42dcb1be8f0a9ec38fafb43488264d3df153bb488fc667eb2a8307d578f1e345" ;
    cof:pageNumber "162"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-141-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-141-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-141-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022-sec-141-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf> ;
    dc:source "data-availability-and-transparency-act-2022.pdf, p.162" .
